// ====================================================================================================================
//
// This json file defines an array of driver ranges for each renderer and platform.
// Each object in the list defines a driver range between min (optional) and max to be blacklisted if the attribute is "blocked"=true
// and/or max driver to be printed by the application as recommended driver version if the attribute is "recommended"=true.
// There might be multiple recommended driver versions for different driver categories (GameReady, RTX/Quadro, etc.)
// Users may enumerate all driver ranges with the attribute of "recommended"=true to determine the recommended driver for the current OV branch/project.
//
// ======= Attributes =================================================================================================
//
// version (64bit integer):
//  - The version for the format of this json file. Always check the version before parsing this file.
//
// Supported platform attributes (platform string with array of driver ranges as the value):
//   - "windows-x86_64"
//   - "linux-x86_64"
//   - "linux-aarch64"
//   Notes:
//     If linux-aarch64 item is not found, linux-x86_64 range array requirements will be used instead.
//     If the intention is to allow all drivers for linux-aarch64 platform, simply define it in this file as empty array: "linux-aarch64": []
//
// blocked (boolean):
//    - If true, the application will block and blacklist the specified driver range [min, max) for the corresponding renderer.
//      Range comparison is as "min <= current-driver < max", which excludes the max value for blocking the range.
//      If a user has installed a driver in that range, the renderer will fail with the "message" string specified as the reason of the failure.
//  
// recommended (boolean):
//    - If true, the driver version listed in the "max" range is the recommended driver for the corresponding "category" and the renderer.
//      Enumerate all the drivers with recommended=true status and check the "category" to find the recommended driver for your desired GPU.
//      Users are encouraged to install this driver, since it is certified for OV and extensively tested.
//  
// category (array of strings):
//    - An array to determine what driver models (BU) the range belongs to. The valid strings in the array are as follows:
//        - "GameReady":  Geforce Game Ready drivers. (e.g. Geforce RTX 5090)
//        - "Studio":     Geforce Studio drivers suitable for creative 3D applications. (e.g. Geforce RTX 5090)
//        - "RTX/Quadro": Workstation UDA drivers for RTX or Quadro GPUs or certain data center GPUs with display mode support. (e.g. A6000/A40/L40)
//        - "Grid/vGPU":  Enterprise drivers for Data Center/Tesla or Grid/vGPU that require a valid license. (e.g. L40)
//
// architecture (array of strings):
//    - An optional array to determine what chip architectures the range belongs to. Otherwise, all architectures are considered.
//      The valid strings in the array are as follows (case sensitive):
//      - "Kepler", "Maxwell", "Pascal", "Volta", "Turing", "Ampere", "Ada", "Hopper", "Blackwell", "T23x" : known chip architectures.
//      - "Unknown" : Any other unknown chip or something newer in the future.
//
// device-id (string):
//    - A string in the format of hexadecimal with prefix 0x (e.g. "0x26b1") or an integer value as string (e.g. "9905") for the specified range.
//      Limitation: It should only be specified if it has a higher min requirement in comparison to another range listed for the same architecture.
//
// min (object):
//    - The minimum NVIDIA driver range to verify or recommend in the format of { "major": 0, "minor": 0, "patch": 0, "build": 0 }
//      for a desired driver version "major.minor.patch.build". For example driver "535.129.03.
//      "min" object is optional. if not specified, assume a value of zero for the driver version.
//
// max (object):
//    - The maximum NVIDIA driver range to verify which excludes the max value itself during comparison as [min, max), or to be the recommend driver,
//      both in the format of { "major": 0, "minor": 0, "patch": 0, "build": 0 } for a desired driver version of "major.minor.patch.build".
//      Attributes of "blocked" and "recommended" determines the action for the range.
//      A range can be blocked from min driver all the way prior to max driver as [min, max).
//      The max driver can also be tagged as the recommended version, since it won't be blocked in the range.
// 
// message (string):
//    - When "blocked" attribute is set to true, it will be the reason for blacklisting the driver range.
//      Otherwise, it is an optional message for attributes such as "recommended" driver, which may not be necessarily displayed by the application. 
//
// url (string):
//  - The optional URL to download the driver from. It can be a link starting with "http:" or "https:",
//    or a path to a network storage starting with "cifs:"
//
// ====================================================================================================================
